      "text": "## The Big Picture"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#002",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:00-overview, git-history:virology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Viruses are obligate intracellular parasites — they have no metabolism of their own,\nno ribosomes, and cannot reproduce outside a host cell. They are not alive in the\ntraditional sense; they are sophisticated nucleic acid delivery systems with protein\nshells. This distinction shapes everything about virology."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:00-overview, git-history:virology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    VIROLOGY LANDSCAPE                            │\n│                                                                  │\n│  WHAT VIRUSES ARE:                 WHAT VIRUSES ARE NOT:         │\n│  ─────────────────                 ─────────────────────         │\n│  Nucleic acid (RNA or DNA)         Not cells                     │\n│  + protein coat (capsid)           No ribosomes                  │\n│  + sometimes a lipid envelope      No ATP synthesis              │\n│  Obligate intracellular            No protein synthesis outside  │\n│  Genome 2-200 kb range            host                           │\n│                                    Not universally \"alive\"       │\n│                                                                  │\n│  CLASSIFICATION:                                                 │\n│  ─────────────────                                               │\n│  Baltimore system (1971) — based on genome type + replication    │\n│  7 classes: I-VII (dsDNA → ssRNA → retroviruses → dsRNA)         │\n│                                                                  │\n│  HOST RANGE:                                                     │\n│  ─────────────                                                   │\n│  Bacteriophage (bacteria) · Animal viruses · Plant viruses       │\n│  Archaeal viruses · Giant viruses (Mimivirus, ~1.2 Mb genome)    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
    },
