      "text": "### The Minimal Virus Problem"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#010",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:00-overview, git-history:virology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "virology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "virology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Virology - Landscape and Taxonomy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A minimal virus must encode:\n1. Capsid proteins (self-assembly)\n2. Some replication machinery (unless relying entirely on host)\n3. Proteins for entry (receptor binding, membrane fusion if enveloped)\n4. Proteins for immune evasion (optional in some viruses)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#011",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:virology:00-overview, git-history:virology:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "virology/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:virology:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
